{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L166","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":166,"end":166}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":166,"end":166},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:4ca4edc7ea2874630c32c1b52c18addca02650a70e183976b2d010ec8602af0d","meta":{"text":"Look up a client adapter by id."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L173","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":173,"end":175}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":173,"end":175},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:fe568e5bea18847e7aac26516f36abe7c6d027beebc5e7fdb8eae970114dfb2e","meta":{"text":"Resolve the skill install destination for a client (or `null` if it has no skill mechanism). Falls\nback to `os.homedir()` (getpwuid on POSIX) when no `home` is passed — never `process.env.HOME ?? ''`,\nwhich yields a relative path (`.claude/skills`) when HOME is unset (sandboxed CI / `env -i`)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L182","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":182,"end":182}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":182,"end":182},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3ccab3674ba64fec296e3646e4ae67db2c6b20d646082e8ac9b9b8040f093e97","meta":{"text":"Read a file as text, or `''` if absent."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L187","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":187,"end":192}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":187,"end":192},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:4fe3cfc87aaeb89866330ba52071d1afd3624c3bb09e2cdf08aff358d5883a2a","meta":{"text":"Splice the managed block into `content`, replacing any existing complete block in place (never\nduplicating). Content outside a COMPLETE marker pair is preserved (a separating newline is inserted\nonly when sibling text directly abuts a marker, so the block stays a standalone region). When a begin\nmarker is present with no matching end marker (a truncated/corrupted file), the function REFUSES to\nsplice and returns `content` unchanged — it cannot know where the block ended, so it must not guess\n(guessing would discard the unterminated tail). The caller observes `written:false` and can repair."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L20","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":20,"end":23}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":20,"end":23},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2e92b5965d34ee156c23f1be27e78854a93ab81c96543480b816392f895e5008","meta":{"text":"A supported agent client for the instruction-adapter registry. A superset of {@link McpIde}:\nincludes `'copilot'` (GitHub Copilot), which has its own instruction file\n(`.github/copilot-instructions.md`) but reuses VS Code's MCP config — so it is a client here but NOT\nan MCP installer target."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L207","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":207,"end":209}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":207,"end":209},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:acfc99afe5719d9b36903efdcc18a496df30852c431ffda347032ccb47ae936a","meta":{"text":"Remove the managed block from `content`, preserving everything outside a COMPLETE marker pair. When\na begin marker is present with no matching end marker, returns `content` unchanged (refuses to remove\n— cannot find the block boundary without discarding the unterminated tail)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L220","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":220,"end":222}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":220,"end":222},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:b823817c8aa265679ad05c762669d68d29aab3b709fd66d858e1a47fc6c5c5ee","meta":{"text":"True if `content` is empty or ONLY YAML frontmatter (no user body). CRLF-tolerant (`\\r?\\n`) so a\nWindows-edited frontmatter-only Cursor rule is still recognized. Only meaningful for `.mdc` targets\n(crib owns the frontmatter it writes there); see `removeInstructions` for the format gate."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L242","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":242,"end":243}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":242,"end":243},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:62c969e72d451574b6bcb2b2b86f36fcd01b0c1aec05f0b5b8e6f2c2ce677bdc","meta":{"text":"Install/refresh the neutral-protocol managed block for one client (or all). Non-destructive:\nsibling content outside the markers is preserved."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L295","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":295,"end":295}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":295,"end":295},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:9b7c9de3881ef22739e5c5caa350f42678e3ca8d1f35a525bec7c207640b770d","meta":{"text":"Report the current managed-block status for each client's instruction file, without writing."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L315","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":315,"end":316}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":315,"end":316},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:fc86f27ff8527632e70a0a49915180c65c75e591b9e82747eb4106da749f25d6","meta":{"text":"Remove the managed block for one client (or all). A crib-owned rule file left empty or\nfrontmatter-only after removal is deleted; a file with remaining user content is left intact."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L62","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":62,"end":67}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":62,"end":67},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:474d42e4cc635fb9ec926c132b769e18519d4b60e2ebf83c5de085a7e16330f2","meta":{"text":"The neutral protocol body — the SAME content for every client's instruction file and the root\n`AGENTS.md`. Vendor-neutral: names the `brief` MCP tool (not a client-specific command), states the\nrecord-only-reusable-learnings rule, the admissible-evidence/no-self-evaluation rule, and the\nnon-destructive rule (memory is not in this file). Exported so tests assert it without re-deriving."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/cli/src/adapters.ts@L91","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":91,"end":91}},"file":"packages/cli/src/adapters.ts","span":{"start":91,"end":91},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:4862705cae5916101ec5793b36685647c8d5b1cd2445da930d50ecac21ccd7b6","meta":{"text":"The full managed block (markers + body) spliced into each instruction file."}}
